<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="Claude" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
  <metadata><name>NE lakes · Day 1 · Vilnius → Zarasai</name></metadata>
  <rte>
    <name>NE lakes · Day 1 · Vilnius → Zarasai</name>
    <rtept lat="54.687200" lon="25.279700"><name>01 Vilnius</name><desc>Fill up before you leave. Swap this point for your own address in Kurviger.</desc></rtept>
    <rtept lat="55.059500" lon="25.444100"><name>02 Dubingiai castle hill</name><desc>Radziwiłł castle site on a peninsula of Lake Asveja, Lithuania&#x27;s longest lake. Walk up for the view over the bridge.</desc></rtept>
    <rtept lat="55.224000" lon="25.405400"><name>03 Molėtai – Viada fuel</name><desc>Last convenient big fuel stop before the park. Top up here; the Himalayan&#x27;s range is fine, but stations get sparse past Labanoras.</desc></rtept>
    <rtept lat="55.219100" lon="25.560900"><name>04 Labanoras park observation tower</name><desc>The tall steel tower by Lake Siesartis, one of the best lake panoramas in the country. Free, 2 min walk from the car park.</desc></rtept>
    <rtept lat="55.269400" lon="25.772700"><name>05 Labanoras visitor centre</name><desc>Good interactive exhibit on the forest and lakes. Ask staff which forest roads are open to vehicles this weekend.</desc></rtept>
    <rtept lat="55.329000" lon="26.102200"><name>06 Palūšė</name><desc>Park HQ and the 1750 wooden St Joseph&#x27;s church on Lake Lūšiai. Pick up the park map and ask about open campsites here.</desc></rtept>
    <rtept lat="55.366400" lon="25.990700"><name>07 Ladakalnis</name><desc>The park&#x27;s signature hill. Six lakes visible from the top. Short climb from the roadside parking.</desc></rtept>
    <rtept lat="55.385500" lon="25.994900"><name>08 Ginučiai watermill</name><desc>The only mill in the park that kept its original machinery. Ginučiai hillfort is right beside it.</desc></rtept>
    <rtept lat="55.381300" lon="25.974400"><name>09 Bičiuliai (Šiliniškės) tower</name><desc>Old telecom mast turned into a 30 m viewing platform. Free, parking at the base.</desc></rtept>
    <rtept lat="55.408500" lon="25.944800"><name>10 Stripeikiai beekeeping museum</name><desc>Ancient Beekeeping Museum with a café. You reach it on the park&#x27;s gravel road via the Papliaušys hollow pine.</desc></rtept>
    <rtept lat="55.448100" lon="25.869800"><name>11 Taurapilis hillfort</name><desc>View over Tauragnas, Lithuania&#x27;s deepest lake (60.5 m). No proper car park, so pull in carefully by the road.</desc></rtept>
    <rtept lat="55.579800" lon="26.134200"><name>12 Salakas</name><desc>Small town between big lakes. Quick stretch before the last leg into Zarasai.</desc></rtept>
    <rtept lat="55.728100" lon="26.243800"><name>13 Zarasai observation circle</name><desc>The curved boardwalk over Lake Zarasas. Arrive with about an hour of daylight to spare, then check in.</desc></rtept>
  </rte>
</gpx>
